                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                        "entry_id": "307f8704-a483-32d5-a074-d4d1dbca75eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Person, die für Zeitungen oder das Radio arbeitet und Bürgern, die ihre oft sehr persönlichen Probleme in einem Leserbrief oder einer E-Mail der Redaktion mitteilten, Ratschläge dazu gibt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "52546c03-5009-44aa-b281-3d1706d87cbb",
                                "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                                "text": "Hast Du schon mal einen Brief an eine Kummerkastentante geschrieben?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63af5955-86b2-4b38-aab2-3a6f222105a4",
                                "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                                "text": "„Eines der Herzstücke jeder Ausgabe sind nach wie vor die Ratgeberseiten. Christiane Fenske[…:] »Salopp gesagt bin ich die Kummerkastentante der Zeitschrift«, sagt sie.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8e4836b-9a92-4302-b0da-997a37a67d98",
                                "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                                "text": "„Für Millionen DDR-Teenies war sie die Kummerkastentante in Liebesdingen. […] Jetzt ist Jutta Resch-Treuwerth mit 73 Jahren an Krebs gestorben.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef503127-e432-4080-a818-b0aa8608e818",
                                "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                                "text": "Und was macht so ein Ombudsmann? Die Tätigkeit ist weniger lustig als der Name. Im Grunde ist P. Nikiforos Diamandouros die Kummerkastentante für 450 000 000 EU-Bürger. Die dürfen sich nämlich mit Beschwerden über sämtliche EU-Institutionen und nationale Behörden an den Bürgerbeauftragten wenden […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e670c69d-3c16-4ce5-b6ec-2b10a97aab86",
                                "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                                "text": "„Der Übersetzer Dieter E. Zimmer gibt im Manesse Verlag die vier Romane von Nathaniel West neu heraus. Nun liegt „Miss Lonelyhearts“ vor, die Geschichte der männlichen Kummerkastentante einer Zeitung, deren Leben aus den Fugen gerärt.“ [Anmerkung: 'gerärt' ist eine Falschschreibung, gemeint ist gerät]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72b9b0e6-1499-4930-9492-9ef550d8e19e",
                                "sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                                "text": "„Die 22-jährige Emmeline möchte Kriegsreporterin werden, kriegt aber nur eine Anstellung als Sekretärin bei der Kummerkastentante einer Frauenzeitschrift.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c6a8253-0e91-45a2-81d3-677650f587e9",
                        "source_entry_id": "307f8704-a483-32d5-a074-d4d1dbca75eb",
                        "source_sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                        "source_sense_description": "Person, die in Medien auf Anfragen Ratschläge erteilt",
                        "target_lang_word": "agony aunt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agony aunt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abd79706-dd2b-3240-9613-346634e949ec",
                                        "entry_id": "f7547775-aa1f-36c1-8f35-ebc29fcd420f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A writer of an advice column in a newspaper or other periodical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db7177e0-3811-41d7-bf49-2ea2a0ff772e",
                                                "sense_id": "abd79706-dd2b-3240-9613-346634e949ec",
                                                "text": "You should write in to the agony aunt; she'll sort it out for you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96ae4fee-a6bb-49bd-ab47-972a3ba6bc35",
                                                "sense_id": "abd79706-dd2b-3240-9613-346634e949ec",
                                                "text": "Pandora has just left my bedroom. I am just about devastated with frustration. I can't go on like this. I have written to Aunt Clara, the Agony Aunt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1f71768-279b-4834-b736-b9b211832072",
                                                "sense_id": "abd79706-dd2b-3240-9613-346634e949ec",
                                                "text": "The big difference between agony aunts then and today is that now we have the internet to answer those tricky problems about how to eat an avocado pear (a lot of letters in the 70s were avocado-related)[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73b7b6fc-eb4a-30ca-a0f6-75c4cd30bdf4",
                                        "entry_id": "f7547775-aa1f-36c1-8f35-ebc29fcd420f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone commonly consulted for advice about personal problems."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58c59536-73c3-41fc-8880-d06f907807c3",
                                                "sense_id": "73b7b6fc-eb4a-30ca-a0f6-75c4cd30bdf4",
                                                "text": "I'm sick of everyone coming to me with their problems—I never wanted to be an agony aunt!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28d1336b-1889-41b4-8a1f-6a9ca3c10f45",
                        "source_entry_id": "307f8704-a483-32d5-a074-d4d1dbca75eb",
                        "source_sense_id": "111bf726-7dd0-3f6e-b482-437e88101c35",
                        "source_sense_description": "Person, die in Medien auf Anfragen Ratschläge erteilt",
                        "target_lang_word": "advice columnist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "advice columnist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f602dc2f-5bd2-3281-9cfe-063f930ab2e9",
                                        "entry_id": "0bb7a8c7-249f-3333-941b-bf973eba4334",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who regularly writes for the advice column of a newspaper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e974bbcc-220f-4328-ba8d-6990bc7f8c74",
                                                "sense_id": "f602dc2f-5bd2-3281-9cfe-063f930ab2e9",
                                                "text": "The columns consist of letters from men and women with problems, followed by brief answers from the advice columnist. The letters are often filled with emotion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f95e4cde-ec2d-4faf-87f1-7d2ea80197de",
                                                "sense_id": "f602dc2f-5bd2-3281-9cfe-063f930ab2e9",
                                                "text": "Ann Landers, who sometimes wrote her columns from her bathtub, called herself “the general manager of the world,” which pretty much describes the types of questions an advice columnist might be called upon to answer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24c126fd-d81d-4850-9330-fc7ded9b2009",
                                                "sense_id": "f602dc2f-5bd2-3281-9cfe-063f930ab2e9",
                                                "text": "Margaret Maron, author of Winter's Child \"A really plummy mystery, flawlessly plotted, that I especially loved because the heroine is an advice columnist — and a good one!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dee9326-96d9-4023-b4ab-2d23f7e566f7",
                                                "sense_id": "f602dc2f-5bd2-3281-9cfe-063f930ab2e9",
                                                "text": "Readers, at least contemporary ones, are aware that writing to an advice columnist is an odd place to turn for help. They didn't doubt, however, that people still wrote to advice columns."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
